<section class="section section-border"><div class="container"><div class="section-header reveal"><div><span class="eyebrow"><span class="section-number">02 / </span> HOW I THINK</span><h2 class="section-heading">Three disciplines. One approach.</h2><p class="section-description">The best solutions are neither purely statistical nor purely engineered. They require a considered balance of all three.</p></div></div>
<div class="approach-grid">
  <div class="approach-card reveal"><span class="approach-num">01 — UNDERSTAND</span><div class="approach-icon">◌</div><h3>Scientific rigor</h3><p>Formulate the right question. Establish useful baselines. Evaluate with realistic validation rather than convenient metrics.</p></div>
  <div class="approach-card reveal"><span class="approach-num">02 — BUILD</span><div class="approach-icon">⌘</div><h3>Engineering discipline</h3><p>Turn experiments into reproducible pipelines, resilient applications, and data products that teams can rely on.</p></div>
  <div class="approach-card reveal"><span class="approach-num">03 — DELIVER</span><div class="approach-icon">↗</div><h3>Decision impact</h3><p>Keep the decision-maker in focus: usability, transparency, maintainability, and the limits of what models can claim.</p></div>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section section-border"><div class="container statement"><div class="reveal"><span class="eyebrow"><span class="section-number">03 / </span> PERSPECTIVE</span><h2>More than a model.<br/>A system people can use.</h2><a class="ghost-link" href="/about/">Learn about my background ↗</a></div><div class="reveal"><div class="quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</div><p class="feature-quote">A strong model is only the beginning. The harder work is connecting it to trustworthy data, meaningful evaluation, and a decision someone can act on.</p><p>My interests sit at the intersection of applied science and software engineering—from retail demand forecasting and operational analytics to natural-language interfaces and multimodal research.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section section-border"><div class="container"><div class="section-header reveal"><div><span class="eyebrow"><span class="section-number">04 / </span> RESEARCH &amp; WRITING</span><h2 class="section-heading">Ideas worth explaining.</h2><p class="section-description">Selected topics and an archive of earlier Jupyter notebook writing. New technical deep-dives will connect directly to the project work.</p></div><a class="ghost-link" href="/writing/">Browse writing ↗</a></div>
<div class="writing-grid">
<a href="/work/forecasting/" class="writing-card reveal"><span class="card-category">Applied methods</span><h3>Forecast validation in the real world</h3><p>How temporal backtesting, baseline comparisons, and error analysis shape forecasting decisions.</p><span class="bottom">Read project notes ↗</span></a>
<a href="/work/speech-research/" class="writing-card reveal"><span class="card-category">Research notes</span><h3>Evaluating multimodal speech features</h3><p>Representation choice, leakage prevention, and grouped validation for speech-based classification.</p><span class="bottom">Read project notes ↗</span></a>
<a href="https://leonardodecastro.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="writing-card reveal"><span class="card-category">Notebook archive</span><h3>Earlier data science writing</h3><p>My original notebook-based technical blog remains available while I curate and migrate selected pieces.</p><span class="bottom">Open original blog ↗</span></a>
</div></div></section>
<div class="container cta-section"><div class="cta-panel reveal"><div><span class="eyebrow">LET'S TALK ABOUT THE HARD PROBLEMS</span><h2>Curious what we could build?</h2><p>I'm interested in thoughtful conversations about applied ML, forecasting, research, and engineering systems that deliver useful outcomes.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
<script is:inline>
  (() => {
   const patterns = {
    seasonal:{a:[47,58,49,75,61,81,68,90,76,95,84,97],p:[50,56,52,70,60,78,69,86,79,92,85,94],note:'Recurring peaks and troughs'},
    intermittent:{a:[0,0,24,0,0,47,0,0,18,0,55,0],p:[7,9,16,8,10,27,11,10,18,12,32,12],note:'Sparse demand and sudden spikes'},
    trending:{a:[20,25,28,32,39,43,46,52,59,66,72,81],p:[21,24,28,34,37,42,47,53,58,64,69,78],note:'Sustained trend and model lag'}
   };
   const X = i => 35 + i*45; const Y = v => 220 - v*1.8;
   const path = vals => vals.map((v,i)=>(i?'L':'M')+X(i)+' '+Y(v).toFixed(1)).join(' ');
   document.querySelectorAll('[data-pattern]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
     const p=patterns[button.dataset.pattern]; if(!p)return;
     document.querySelectorAll('[data-pattern]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button)));
     document.querySelectorAll('#chart-actual').forEach(el=>el.setAttribute('d',path(p.a)));
     document.querySelectorAll('#chart-predict').forEach(el=>el.setAttribute('d',path(p.p)));
     document.querySelectorAll('#chart-fill').forEach(el=>el.setAttribute('d',path(p.a)+' L530 222 L35 222 Z'));
     document.querySelectorAll('#last-marker').forEach(el=>{el.setAttribute('cx',String(X(11)));el.setAttribute('cy',String(Y(p.a[11])))});
     const label=document.getElementById('pattern-note');if(label)label.textContent=p.note;
   }));
  })();
</script>

</SiteLayout>
